CAT = "hkle1Law"; SEG = "LAW"
Q = [
("Hong Kong's legal system is based mainly on:",
 "The common law", ["Civil code law", "Islamic law", "Customary clan law"],
 "Under the Basic Law, Hong Kong keeps the common law system it had before 1997, alongside its own ordinances and rules of equity."),
("Which court is Hong Kong's final appellate court?",
 "The Court of Final Appeal", ["The Court of First Instance", "The District Court", "The Court of Appeal"],
 "The Court of Final Appeal hears final appeals. The High Court is made up of the Court of Appeal and the Court of First Instance."),
("Compared with a court case, arbitration is usually:",
 "Private and binding", ["Public and open to the press", "Decided by a jury of citizens", "Only advisory and never binding"],
 "Parties agree to refer disputes to an arbitrator, the hearing is private, and the award is binding and enforceable under the Arbitration Ordinance."),
("Under the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622), a private company must:",
 "Restrict transfer of its shares", ["List its shares on the exchange", "Have at least seven members", "Offer its shares to the public"],
 "A private company restricts share transfers, limits its members to 50 (excluding employees) and may not invite the public to subscribe for its shares."),
("A company limited by guarantee is typically formed for:",
 "Non-profit purposes", ["Raising capital from investors", "Listing on the GEM board", "Running a family trading business"],
 "Members of a guarantee company promise a fixed contribution on winding up and it has no share capital, so it suits clubs, charities and other non-profit bodies."),
("Since the Companies Ordinance (Cap. 622) took effect in 2014, Hong Kong companies' shares:",
 "Have no par or nominal value", ["Must have a par value", "Must be bearer shares", "Cannot be issued at a premium"],
 "Cap. 622 moved all local companies with a share capital to a no-par regime, so share premium and par value no longer apply."),
("Which resolution needs at least 75% of the votes cast?",
 "A special resolution", ["An ordinary resolution", "A board resolution", "A written directors' minute"],
 "An ordinary resolution passes by a simple majority, and a special resolution needs at least 75% of the votes. Changing the articles is a typical special resolution."),
("Which document sets out a Hong Kong company's internal rules after Cap. 622?",
 "The articles of association", ["The memorandum of association", "The certificate of registration", "The annual return"],
 "Cap. 622 abolished the memorandum's role for new companies; a company's constitution is its articles of association."),
("A debenture is best described as:",
 "A record of company debt", ["A share carrying extra votes", "A director's service contract", "A dividend warrant"],
 "A debenture evidences a loan to the company, often secured by a charge on its assets. Holders are creditors, not members."),
("A director must exercise reasonable care, skill and diligence. In Hong Kong this duty is:",
 "Written into statute", ["Owed only to the creditors", "Removed if the director is unpaid", "Found only in the articles"],
 "Cap. 622 states the director's duty of care, skill and diligence in statute, measured by an objective and a subjective standard. Fiduciary duties continue at common law."),
("A director who secretly profits from a deal with the company most likely breaches:",
 "Fiduciary duty", ["The duty to file returns", "The quorum rule", "The duty to keep a seal"],
 "Directors owe fiduciary duties to the company to act in good faith and avoid conflicts; an undisclosed profit must be accounted for to the company."),
("A minority shareholder whose interests are unfairly prejudiced by how the company is run can ask the court for:",
 "An unfair prejudice order", ["A cold shoulder order", "A restriction notice", "A licence suspension order"],
 "The Companies Ordinance lets a member petition the court where the company's affairs are conducted in an unfairly prejudicial way; the court has wide remedial powers."),
("A derivative action is brought by a shareholder:",
 "On behalf of the company", ["For their own lost dividend", "Against the SFC", "To wind up a solvent company"],
 "In a derivative action a member sues for a wrong done to the company, such as a director's breach, when those in control will not act. Any recovery goes to the company."),
("Who may appoint inspectors to investigate the affairs of a Hong Kong company?",
 "The Financial Secretary", ["The company secretary", "The Insurance Authority", "Any creditor acting alone"],
 "Under the Companies Ordinance the Financial Secretary may appoint inspectors to investigate a company's affairs, for example on members' application or where fraud is suspected."),
("A solvent company's directors make a declaration of solvency and the members resolve to wind it up. This is a:",
 "Members' voluntary winding up", ["Creditors' voluntary winding up", "Compulsory winding up", "Scheme of arrangement"],
 "With a declaration of solvency the members control a voluntary liquidation. Without one it becomes a creditors' voluntary winding up, and a court order is a compulsory winding up."),
("A company is wound up by order of the court on a creditor's petition. This is a:",
 "Compulsory winding up", ["Members' voluntary winding up", "Creditors' voluntary winding up", "Deregistration"],
 "A winding up ordered by the court, usually on a creditor's petition because the company cannot pay its debts, is a compulsory winding up."),
]
